{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSaH8VxEpSxJE4XZmHex","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders, cancels associated CREATED shipments, handles error cases properly (including idempotent retry), and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       \n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order data class\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST cancel endpoint with full logic for cancellation, error handling, and shipment cascade\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId(orderId) method to retrieve shipments for an order\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders with 409\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 new tests covering cancel functionality (ACTIVE→CANCELLED, idempotent retry, 409 with CONFIRMED shipment, 404 for missing order, cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments)\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 2 new tests for shipment creation rejection on cancelled orders and success on non-existent orders\n\nTests       \n- created order has ACTIVE status: Verifies new orders are ACTIVE (AC1, AC3)\n- cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status: Verifies cancel returns 200 with CANCELLED status (AC3)\n- cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds with idempotent response: Verifies idempotent retry succeeds without error (AC5)\n- cancelling a non-existent order returns 404: Verifies 404 ResourceNotFoundException (AC5)\n- cancelling an order with a confirmed shipment returns 409 and changes nothing: Verifies 409 ConflictException, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED (AC5)\n- cancelling an order cancels all created shipments: Verifies cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments (AC3)\n- rejects shipment creation for cancelled order with 409: Verifies 409 ORDER_CANCELLED when creating shipment for cancelled order (AC5)\n- allows shipment creation for non-existent order: Verifies current behavior preserved for non-existent orders (AC5)\n- All existing tests (4 OrderControllerTest + 5 ShipmentControllerTest): Pass unchanged to verify no regression\n\nVerification  Ran `./mvnw test` from sample-service/: BUILD SUCCESS with 21 tests passing (10 OrderControllerTest, 7 ShipmentControllerTest, 3 CustomerControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests)\n\nNot done      None. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no forbidden files changed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":907,"cache_read_input_tokens":42764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":907},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cced31fe-3160-4f89-9549-305ab5c4f960","uuid":"bcd7e8f7-941a-4e78-874f-318729d1130f","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:06:49.589Z","request_id":"req_011CfSaH83RKy9kPDMyjYT8d"}
